      "writtenOn": "2020-10-28T16:30:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dino, I really think we can avoid adding the new functions (e.g. interrupt_enable_arch) and make the existing interrupt_enable and interrupt_disable allow for nesting (similar to Ed\u0027s testing CL:1940783).\n\nI think we can just make a very similar change in all of the core files to have a counter for the number of nested interrupt disable calls. That way all existing code gets to take advantage of these nesting interrupts and we don\u0027t have to have a special set of functions for that.\n\nWhat are your thoughts on this approach?",
      "parentUuid": "28c8ea8c_3111ea64",
      "revId": "72cfb665368c5303448c5ed61b477afb240603cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
